happen to be Alpha powered and run a proprietary embedded OS and use an
OpenBoot firmware (as opposed to SRM or the now dead AlphaBIOS).  This is
the same firmware as modern UltraSPARC and PowerPC/Power3 machines use
(which means they all can use the same boot device drivers, remote boot
code, diagnostics, etc, at the firmware level).

